<?php
/* Failover Guard — settings page.
   Bilingual on purpose: this box is used by people who read either language. */

$plugin  = "failover-guard";
$cfgfile = "/boot/config/plugins/$plugin/config";
$script  = "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/$plugin/scripts/failover-guard";

$cfg = file_exists($cfgfile) ? parse_ini_file($cfgfile) : [];
function v($cfg, $k, $d = "") { return htmlspecialchars($cfg[$k] ?? $d); }

$status = json_decode(shell_exec("bash " . escapeshellarg($script) . " status 2>/dev/null"), true) ?: [];
$switched = ($status['switched'] ?? 'no') === 'yes';
$watcher  = $status['watcher'] ?? 'stopped';
?>

<style>
.fg-state { padding:6px 10px; border-radius:4px; display:inline-block; margin-right:8px; }
.fg-ok    { background:#1a7f37; color:#fff; }
.fg-warn  { background:#9a6700; color:#fff; }
.fg-bad   { background:#b32d2e; color:#fff; }
.fg-note  { opacity:.75; font-size:.9em; }
</style>

<div style="margin-bottom:14px">
  <span class="fg-state <?= $watcher === 'running' ? 'fg-ok' : 'fg-bad' ?>">
    Watcher: <?= $watcher ?>
  </span>
  <span class="fg-state <?= $switched ? 'fg-warn' : 'fg-ok' ?>">
    <?= $switched ? 'FAILED OVER — serving locally / CONMUTADO — sirviendo en local'
                  : 'Normal — origin is serving / Normal — sirve el origen' ?>
  </span>
</div>

<form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.htm" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="<?= $plugin ?>/config">

**Enable failover / Activar el failover:**
: <select name="ENABLED">
  <option value="no"  <?= v($cfg,'ENABLED','no')=='no'  ? 'selected' : '' ?>>No</option>
  <option value="yes" <?= v($cfg,'ENABLED','no')=='yes' ? 'selected' : '' ?>>Yes / Sí</option>
  </select>

> While this is off the watcher stays stopped and nothing is ever switched.
> Mientras esté en No, el vigilante no arranca y nunca se conmuta nada.

### Origin / Origen

**Origin host / Host del origen:**
: <input type="text" name="ORIGIN_HOST" value="<?= v($cfg,'ORIGIN_HOST') ?>" placeholder="vps.example.com">

> The real host name of the remote server, NOT the public domain. If your domain
> sits behind a CDN it answers even when the origin is dead, so it is useless here.
> El nombre real del servidor remoto, NO el dominio público: si el dominio pasa por
> un CDN, responde aunque el origen esté muerto y no sirve para vigilar.

**TCP ports to probe / Puertos TCP a sondear:**
: <input type="text" name="ORIGIN_PORTS" value="<?= v($cfg,'ORIGIN_PORTS','443') ?>" placeholder="22 443">

**Health path / Ruta de salud:**
: <input type="text" name="HEALTH_PATH" value="<?= v($cfg,'HEALTH_PATH') ?>" placeholder="/api/health">

> Optional but strongly recommended: an open port only proves the machine booted,
> not that the site works. Left empty, only ports are checked.
> Opcional pero muy recomendable: un puerto abierto solo demuestra que la máquina
> arrancó, no que el sitio funcione. Vacío, solo se comprueban los puertos.

**Expected in response / Se espera en la respuesta:**
: <input type="text" name="HEALTH_EXPECT" value="<?= v($cfg,'HEALTH_EXPECT') ?>" placeholder='"ok":true'>

### Switching / Conmutación

**Domain / Dominio:**
: <input type="text" name="DOMAIN" value="<?= v($cfg,'DOMAIN') ?>" placeholder="example.com">

**Failover target / Destino del failover:**
: <input type="text" name="FAILOVER_TARGET" value="<?= v($cfg,'FAILOVER_TARGET') ?>" placeholder="home.example.com">

> A host name (becomes a CNAME) or an IP (becomes an A record) pointing at this
> box. A dynamic DNS name with a short TTL works best.
> Un nombre de host (se pone como CNAME) o una IP (registro A) que apunte a este
> servidor. Lo ideal es un nombre de DNS dinámico con TTL corto.

**Cloudflare API token / Token de API de Cloudflare:**
: <input type="password" name="CF_TOKEN" value="<?= v($cfg,'CF_TOKEN') ?>">

> Needs Zone:Read and DNS:Edit on that zone only.
> Necesita Zone:Read y DNS:Edit únicamente sobre esa zona.

**Check interval (s) / Intervalo de comprobación (s):**
: <input type="number" name="CHECK_INTERVAL" min="5" max="600" value="<?= v($cfg,'CHECK_INTERVAL','10') ?>">

**Failures before switching / Fallos antes de conmutar:**
: <input type="number" name="FAIL_THRESHOLD" min="1" max="20" value="<?= v($cfg,'FAIL_THRESHOLD','3') ?>">

> Detection time is roughly interval × failures. Three failures avoids switching
> on a passing network blip.
> El tiempo de detección es aproximadamente intervalo × fallos. Tres fallos evitan
> conmutar por un bache de red pasajero.

### Nginx Proxy Manager (optional / opcional)

**NPM data path / Ruta de datos de NPM:**
: <input type="text" name="NPM_DATA" value="<?= v($cfg,'NPM_DATA') ?>" placeholder="/mnt/user/appdata/NginxProxyManager/data">

**NPM container / Contenedor de NPM:**
: <input type="text" name="NPM_CONTAINER" value="<?= v($cfg,'NPM_CONTAINER','Nginx-Proxy-Manager-Official') ?>">

**Proxy host ID / ID del proxy host:**
: <input type="text" name="NPM_HOST_ID" value="<?= v($cfg,'NPM_HOST_ID') ?>" placeholder="65">

> The local host stays disabled while the origin is healthy, so two copies never
> accept writes at the same time. It is enabled only during a failover.
> El host local permanece deshabilitado mientras el origen está sano, para que
> nunca haya dos copias aceptando escrituras. Solo se habilita durante un failover.

### Data hooks / Enganches de datos

**Replicate hook / Enganche de réplica:**
: <input type="text" name="HOOK_REPLICATE" value="<?= v($cfg,'HOOK_REPLICATE') ?>" placeholder="/boot/config/plugins/failover-guard/replicate.sh">

**Pre-failback hook / Enganche previo al failback:**
: <input type="text" name="HOOK_PRE_FAILBACK" value="<?= v($cfg,'HOOK_PRE_FAILBACK') ?>" placeholder="/boot/config/plugins/failover-guard/failback.sh">

> This plugin never touches your data — only you know what your data is. The
> replicate hook copies origin → here while all is well. The pre-failback hook
> copies here → origin before returning, and it runs with the local host already
> disabled, so nothing can be written mid-copy. If it fails, the failback is
> aborted and this box keeps serving.
> El plugin no toca tus datos: solo tú sabes cuáles son. El enganche de réplica
> copia origen → aquí mientras todo va bien. El de pre-failback copia aquí →
> origen antes de volver, y se ejecuta con el host local ya deshabilitado, así que
> nada puede escribirse a mitad de copia. Si falla, el failback se aborta y este
> servidor sigue sirviendo.

**Replicate interval (s) / Intervalo de réplica (s):**
: <input type="number" name="REPLICATE_INTERVAL" min="300" value="<?= v($cfg,'REPLICATE_INTERVAL','3600') ?>">

**Notifications / Notificaciones:**
: <select name="NOTIFY">
  <option value="yes" <?= v($cfg,'NOTIFY','yes')=='yes' ? 'selected' : '' ?>>Yes / Sí</option>
  <option value="no"  <?= v($cfg,'NOTIFY','yes')=='no'  ? 'selected' : '' ?>>No</option>
  </select>

&nbsp;
: <input type="submit" value="Apply / Aplicar"><input type="button" value="Done / Hecho" onclick="done()">

</form>

### Checks / Comprobaciones

<pre id="fgtest" style="max-height:260px;overflow:auto">Press the button to run every check without changing anything.
Pulsa el botón para ejecutar todas las comprobaciones sin cambiar nada.</pre>

<input type="button" value="Run checks / Comprobar" onclick="fgTest()">

### Log / Registro

<pre id="fglog" style="max-height:420px;overflow:auto">Loading… / Cargando…</pre>

<input type="button" value="Refresh / Actualizar" onclick="fgLog()">
<input type="button" value="Clear / Vaciar" onclick="fgClear()">
<label><input type="checkbox" id="fgauto" onchange="fgAuto()"> Auto-refresh (5s) / Auto-actualizar (5s)</label>
<select id="fglines" onchange="fgLog()">
  <option value="100">100</option>
  <option value="200" selected>200</option>
  <option value="500">500</option>
  <option value="2000">2000</option>
</select>

> Full file / Fichero completo: `/var/log/<?= $plugin ?>.log`

<script>
var fgTimer = null;

function fgTest() {
  document.getElementById('fgtest').textContent = 'Running… / Comprobando…';
  $.post('/plugins/<?= $plugin ?>/include/action.php', {action:'test'}, function(d) {
    document.getElementById('fgtest').textContent = d;
  });
}

function fgLog() {
  var n = document.getElementById('fglines').value;
  $.post('/plugins/<?= $plugin ?>/include/action.php', {action:'log', lines:n}, function(d) {
    var box = document.getElementById('fglog');
    // Keep the newest lines in view: that is what you came to read.
    var stuck = (box.scrollTop + box.clientHeight >= box.scrollHeight - 30);
    box.textContent = d;
    if (stuck) box.scrollTop = box.scrollHeight;
  });
}

function fgClear() {
  $.post('/plugins/<?= $plugin ?>/include/action.php', {action:'clearlog'}, function() { fgLog(); });
}

function fgAuto() {
  if (document.getElementById('fgauto').checked) {
    fgTimer = setInterval(fgLog, 5000);
  } else {
    clearInterval(fgTimer); fgTimer = null;
  }
}

$(function() {
  fgLog();
  document.getElementById('fglog').scrollTop = document.getElementById('fglog').scrollHeight;
});
</script>
